<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Lebanon faces uncertainty as UNIFIL mandate nears end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afad535eea7cdf8587737c419b0fc63445dffa736d9ab0b744431a6d095f2714</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491--a12453a4b744.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As UN peacekeeping forces prepare to withdraw from Lebanon, Israel remains present and Hezbollah is still armed. A new EU support mission aims to strengthen Lebanon's army, but will not replace UN peacekeepers.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan drone strike kills around 150 in Abyei market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1a0d6d178bb0971872af574059235646f91b7e013730c3b0688860828167854</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587--6d5e17c39f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone strike hit a market in the Abyei border region disputed by Sudan and South Sudan and killed dozens. The drone caused a large fire when it hit a fuel depot. South Sudanese officials blamed Sudan's military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory, says new report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4db01feb6420ae6a3c0a28088268ccf0f3b32a085fd637b1e3e1eb96a448ad3</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877--a509ee21abbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula, Flavio Bolsonaro tied ahead of runoff vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305538cfe9db421c40dc76da29c6741d7e9697ccdc42192cf139793fe38d7dc5</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182--cfbbc055c58e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With just under a week to go before the decisive presidential runoff election, polls show left-wing incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro are virtually tied.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fbc558b536d901dfdc4f151359d2fc3a0cf3eca217bae80ceb67e50de0fff7</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:044776afd8848d869644602bd285d4ab295db679b446668d357b5c93e6162bf1</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta rejects separation bid, CBC projects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fdd6c760bdbc465dfe6ae377b0ec541a83300690712bd7ad03a1442ab3d8f45</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520--59931f2b4e41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters have decisively rejected a proposal to begin the legal process toward Alberta's independence, dealing a major blow to a movement driven largely by economic grievances.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP seriously hurt in suspected car attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e034d8a67f563946a15987597a96b060f8f693a4176e901366d4180219294810</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660--8ec3224c2b82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Helen Haines, an independent federal lawmaker, suffered severe injuries in what Australia's prime minister has called a deliberate attack by a man in a car.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b37a52bab194f6232d5aee9842eb9fc90732265bc37f849d6241faf20f990f4b</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta votes on holding independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3576b185a6d39fc721d550601d7b89d5fe0d22677820517a6ae2925dfa08c55e</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283--4cfaa44e1aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada's oil-rich western province of Alberta is not deemed likely to vote in favor of a real breakaway plebiscite. Nevertheless the separatist movement hopes to gain leverage over Mark Carney's government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can diplomacy stop another Ethiopia-Eritrea war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caefabe41217f15501f5a15ae53396c20d1ac196c71fa8abbb2bcf0ee67598a4</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-diplomacy-stop-another-ethiopia-eritrea-war/a-79705435--b90ab4301994.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-diplomacy-stop-another-ethiopia-eritrea-war/a-79705435?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia has installed a new administration in conflict-hit Tigray after federal forces pushed back Tigrayan fighters. But tensions with Eritrea continue to raise fears of a wider regional war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio visits India with a trip to the world's largest oil refinery topping the agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43b0561b6179805c15a32437d5f163d7ea6f258e8ab9e2ab620e96c3822a500f</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826--dd280f73407c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visit to India this week by Washington's top diplomat will skip New Delhi and instead include the world's largest oil refinery, which processes massive amounts of Russian crude. Is Trump looking for a new deal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289332c77af63c7efcf204506f2caf599f86d552a33f10e024575bdd345cbe1e</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
